{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310543,"nonce":"+G87ssJ281vjgeucltcptfgmg0w=","title":"BLADE cache cross-test contamination on stdlib properties FIXED (a332319) — orphan property entries with no class shadowed real Method ...","message":"`test_stringbuf_stringtools` failed in batch (passed isolated) when run after `test_exception`. Errors were \"Cannot access field 'length'\" / \"Cannot access field 'trim'\" etc. — 10 distinct field-access errors cascading from a single root.\n\n**Root cause (two parts):**\n\n1. **Save**: `build_cached_maps_from_mir_result` always pushed a `BladePropertyEntry` per `property_access_map` entry, even when `find_class_name_for_scope` returned None — those serialised with `class_name=\"\"`. Three such orphan entries from ArrayKeyValueIterator/ArrayIterator's caches accumulated in the loaded property_access_map.\n\n2. **Lookup**: `lower_field_access`'s name-based property fallback returned the FIRST entry whose symbol name matched. Orphans had `getter=Default`, the real entry had `getter=Method(\"get_length\")` — BTreeMap iteration order surfaced the orphan first, `buf.length` got `Default`, fell through the Method-getter branch, hit the \"Cannot access field\" error path.\n\nThe cascade: StringTools.hx fails to compile (`s.length` on String trips a similar shadow), then every `StringTools.X(...)` static call in user code fails because StringTools' methods never registered.\n\n**Fix (a332319):**\n\n- Save side: skip property entries whose `class_name` is None. Orphan entries can never be restored correctly (load keys by class_name) and only cause shadows.\n- Lookup: name-based fallback in property dispatch now prefers `Method(...)` getters over `Default` ones — Method wins when a real getter exists, Default only when no real property is registered.\n- Defensive third: `resolve_field_index_by_name` returns None when the receiver is an extern class and no candidates match — prevents a cached `StringBuf.length` field index from masquerading as `String.length` etc. on the GEP path.\n\n**Verification:** 128/128 haxe regression (full clean suite, was 127/128). Both `test_exception` and `test_stringbuf_stringtools` pass in batch AND isolation.\n\n**How to apply:** Any new BLADE-cached classes with property accessors will round-trip cleanly. The save-side skip means new orphan-prone classes can't pollute downstream loads. The lookup-side preference means residual orphans from older caches don't shadow legitimate entries either.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_blade_property_orphan` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}